{
  "id": "hot-update",
  "title": "Hot updates while you edit",
  "summary": "A hot update changes the open page while you edit. A stylesheet update keeps the page state. A supported service update stops the service and starts it again. The service gets back the state that it chooses to keep. Only JavaScript and TypeScript services get hot updates. A change to a service in another language reloads the page, and the service starts again with its first values. Python and Lua services reload the same way; a Python service also needs the `tac.python` runtime in the manifest, as the `client/manifest.json` tab shows (ADR 0093). Other changes can need a full page reload. A failed build keeps the last good page and shows a diagnostic overlay (error messages on top of the page) with the file, the line and help. The preview never stops because of a problem in your files: a project that is broken at start gets an error page until a save fixes it.",
  "group": "Tooling",
